/* Slot grid v2: square cells for items, skills and emotions, fed by the slot
   model of assets/root/nui_slots.py (docs/ui/AUTHORING.md "Slot grids").
   Two kinds of grid share the cell: the full cell, with every part (the
   taskbar's quick slots, the skill pickers, the inventory's wear cells,
   which list only the parts they show), and the lean grid of the item
   windows (the bag page, the belt, select item; P14 spec 4.2).

   A full cell, every part (the window's event names; the grid's name first):

   <div class="nui-slot-grid nui-slot-grid--cols-4" id="quick-slots">
   	<div class="nui-slot nui-anim" data-for="slot : quick_slots"
   	     data-class-is-empty="slot.kind == ''"
   	     data-class-is-disabled="slot.disabled" data-class-is-locked="slot.locked"
   	     data-class-is-picked="slot.index == quick_picked"
   	     data-class-is-selected="slot.index == quick_selected"
   	     data-event-mousedown="slot_press('quick', slot.index, ev.button)"
   	     data-event-mouseup="slot_release('quick', slot.index, ev.button)"
   	     data-event-mouseover="slot_over('quick', slot.index)"
   	     data-event-mouseout="slot_out('quick', slot.index)"
   	     data-event-nuidrop="slot_drop('quick', slot.index)">
   		<img class="nui-slot__icon" data-if="slot.icon != ''" data-attr-src="slot.icon"/>
   		<div class="nui-slot__cover" data-if="slot.cover"></div>
   		<div class="nui-slot__tint"></div>
   		<nui-cooldown class="nui-slot__cooldown" data-if="slot.cd_end > 0"
   			data-attr-start="slot.cd_start" data-attr-end="slot.cd_end"/>
   		<nui-frames class="nui-slot__active" data-if="slot.active" count="13" delay="0.0667"/>
   		<span class="nui-slot__ring nui-anim nui-fx" data-if="slot.active" data-class-is-on="slot.active"></span>
   		<nui-frames class="nui-slot__finish" data-if="slot.cd_end > 0" count="11"
   			delay="0.0333" loop="false" after="none" data-attr-start="slot.cd_end"/>
   		<nui-frames class="nui-slot__flash nui-anim" data-if="slot.cd_end > 0" count="11"
   			delay="0.0333" loop="false" after="none" data-attr-start="slot.cd_end"/>
   		<span class="nui-slot__count" data-if="slot.count != ''">{{ slot.count }}</span>
   		<nui-number class="nui-slot__digits" data-if="slot.count != ''" data-attr-value="slot.count"/>
   	</div>
   </div>

   States: is-empty, is-disabled (the legacy red tint), is-locked (the legacy
   black tint; the controller refuses a pick), is-picked (drawn only in a grid
   with nui-slot-grid--pick, as legacy's SLOT_STYLE_PICK_UP), is-selected,
   is-target (a drop footprint cell that the attached item can move to),
   is-blocked (one it cannot), is-usable and is-unusable (use mode: the
   item under an attached refine scroll or stone, P14 spec 4.4),
   is-unavailable (the belt's cells beyond its grade), :hover and is-hover.
   A disabled, locked or unavailable cell keeps its pointer events, as legacy
   cells take clicks. nui-slot--h2, --h3, --w2 and --w3 size a single cell
   that holds a taller or wider item (a wear cell).
   Every part ignores the pointer, so the cell is always the event target and
   moving over its icon sends no mouseout.

   The parts draw in the legacy order (CSlotWindow::OnRender): the pick and
   selection tint under the icon, then the icon, the disabled tint, the
   cooldown sweep, the cover, the count, the finish effect, the active effect
   and the locked tint on top. The cell is a stacking context (z-index 0), so
   a negative z-index draws above its background and under the icon.

   A lean grid (nui-slot-grid--lean): the grid draws every resting cell base
   with one decorator (nui-cells, one mesh and one draw for the whole grid),
   a cell draws nothing at rest, and its markup holds only the parts its
   content can show. Its list is fixed-length (cols x rows cells that never
   change while the document lives), so the repeated cell may read its own
   entry. An item larger than one cell draws from its anchor cell (its top
   cell) over the cells it covers, which stay hit targets (nui_slots
   item_cells, owner_index):

   <div class="nui-slot-grid nui-slot-grid--lean nui-slot-grid--cols-5" id="inv-bag">
   	<div class="nui-slot nui-anim nui-fx" data-for="c : bag" data-attr-id="'inv-bag-' + it_index"
   	     data-class-is-empty="c.kind == '' &amp;&amp; !c.covered" data-class-is-covered="c.covered"
   	     data-class-is-picked="c.picked" data-class-is-active="c.active"
   	     data-class-is-target="c.target == 'move'" data-class-is-blocked="c.target == 'blocked'"
   	     data-class-is-usable="c.target == 'usable'" data-class-is-unusable="c.target == 'unusable'"
   	     data-class-nui-slot--h2="c.h == 2" data-class-nui-slot--h3="c.h == 3"
   	     data-event-mousedown="bag_press(it_index, ev.button)" ...>
   		<img class="nui-slot__icon" data-if="c.icon != ''" data-attr-src="c.icon"/>
   		<nui-number class="nui-slot__number" data-if="c.count != ''" data-attr-value="c.count"/>
   	</div>
   </div>

   The grid is the stacking context (position relative, z-index 0) and a cell
   is positioned without a z-index, so every cell's background paints before
   every part, and a tall item's icon draws above the cells it covers; the
   parts take the legacy order by z-index: icon 1, disabled tint 2,
   cooldown 3, cover 4, count 5, finish 6, active 7, locked tint 8, sign 9.
   nui-slot__number is the lean grid's one count part: nui-number draws its
   text as the count badge in the modern skins and the legacy digits in
   classic. A lean cell's active state is the cell itself (a 2dp accent
   border and a static glow, no motion).

   No dead zones, hover per item (P14b): a cell's hit box reaches half the
   gap to its neighbors (nui-hit-outset, Core/ElementHitOutset.h: the
   pointer sees a div larger than it draws), so the pointer anywhere in a
   grid is over exactly one cell and the drawn cells stay as they were. In
   a lean grid at rest, an anchor's box is its item's whole area, gaps
   included (the negative margin keeps the rows), and the cells it covers
   take no pointer: the pointer anywhere over an item is over its anchor,
   so :hover lights the item as one shape and the tooltip stays up while
   the pointer crosses the item's gaps. While something is attached (the
   grid's is-attaching, which the window sets through nui_slots'
   LegacySlotEvents), every cell is its own target again, so the drop
   footprint follows the cell under the pointer as legacy's does. A grid
   whose cells can hold a multi-cell item binds is-attaching
   (docs/ui/AUTHORING.md "Slot grids").

   Modern: 40dp cells 4dp apart (a 44dp pitch), the 32dp icon 4dp inside.
   The active ring has a static glow (a box-shadow, drawn once), and the
   finish effect is a burst: a radial gradient that scales by transform while
   it plays. Classic (skins/classic/classic.rcss): the legacy 32dp pitch with
   the slot base art (tiled by the lean grid), the legacy tints and cover
   art, the legacy digits and the legacy effect frames. */

.nui-slot-grid
{
	display: flex;
	flex-direction: row;
	flex-wrap: wrap;
	gap: var(--space-1);
}
/* n cells of 40dp and n - 1 gaps of 4dp: the cells wrap into n columns. */
.nui-slot-grid--cols-1 { width: 40dp; }
.nui-slot-grid--cols-2 { width: 84dp; }
.nui-slot-grid--cols-3 { width: 128dp; }
.nui-slot-grid--cols-4 { width: 172dp; }
.nui-slot-grid--cols-5 { width: 216dp; }
.nui-slot-grid--cols-6 { width: 260dp; }
.nui-slot-grid--cols-7 { width: 304dp; }
.nui-slot-grid--cols-8 { width: 348dp; }
.nui-slot-grid--cols-9 { width: 392dp; }
.nui-slot-grid--cols-10 { width: 436dp; }

.nui-slot
{
	display: block;
	position: relative;
	z-index: 0;
	box-sizing: border-box;
	width: 40dp;
	height: 40dp;
	padding: 3dp;
	background-color: var(--surface-sunken);
	border-width: 1dp;
	border-color: var(--border);
	border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
	/* Half the 4dp gap on every side: the cells' hit boxes tile the grid. */
	nui-hit-outset: 2dp;
}
.nui-slot:hover, .nui-slot.is-hover
{
	background-color: var(--surface-hover);
	border-color: var(--accent);
}
.nui-slot.is-selected
{
	border-color: var(--accent);
}
/* The drop footprint (P14 spec 4.4): the cells an attached item would
   cover, white in legacy where it can move, red where it cannot; in use
   mode the target item, yellow where the attached item can be used on it,
   red where it cannot. */
.nui-slot.is-target
{
	background-color: var(--slot-target);
	border-color: var(--accent);
}
.nui-slot.is-blocked
{
	background-color: var(--slot-blocked);
	border-color: var(--danger);
}
.nui-slot.is-usable
{
	background-color: var(--slot-usable);
	border-color: var(--warning);
}
.nui-slot.is-unusable
{
	background-color: var(--slot-unusable);
	border-color: var(--danger);
}
/* A cell beyond the belt's grade: dimmed, with no hover look; it still
   takes the pointer (the server refuses a drop there). */
.nui-slot.is-unavailable, .nui-slot.is-unavailable:hover
{
	background-color: var(--slot-unavailable);
	border-color: var(--border);
}
/* Hover fade (--dur-fast, --ease-out). */
.nui-slot.nui-anim
{
	transition: background-color border-color 0.1s cubic-out;
}
/* A single cell that holds a taller or wider item (a wear cell): its span
   in 44dp steps. */
.nui-slot--h2 { height: 84dp; }
.nui-slot--h3 { height: 128dp; }
.nui-slot--w2 { width: 84dp; }
.nui-slot--w3 { width: 128dp; }

.nui-slot__icon
{
	display: block;
	width: 32dp;
	height: 32dp;
	pointer-events: none;
}
/* A taller item's icon at its own size (32 x 64 or 32 x 96dp), centered in
   the item's area: 10dp or 16dp from its top. */
.nui-slot--h2 > .nui-slot__icon, .nui-slot--h3 > .nui-slot__icon
{
	position: absolute;
	left: 3dp;
	height: auto;
}
.nui-slot--h2 > .nui-slot__icon { top: 9dp; }
.nui-slot--h3 > .nui-slot__icon { top: 15dp; }

/* Skills and emotions: a 1dp ring inside the icon. */
.nui-slot__cover
{
	position: absolute;
	left: 3dp;
	top: 3dp;
	z-index: 3;
	box-sizing: border-box;
	width: 32dp;
	height: 32dp;
	border-width: 1dp;
	border-color: var(--accent);
	border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
	pointer-events: none;
}

/* The tints of the disabled, locked, picked and selected states, over the
   whole cell inside its border. */
.nui-slot__tint
{
	position: absolute;
	left: 0;
	top: 0;
	right: 0;
	bottom: 0;
	pointer-events: none;
}
.nui-slot.is-disabled .nui-slot__tint
{
	z-index: 1;
	background-color: var(--slot-disabled);
}
.nui-slot-grid--pick .nui-slot.is-picked .nui-slot__tint
{
	z-index: -1;
	background-color: var(--slot-picked);
}
.nui-slot.is-locked .nui-slot__tint
{
	z-index: 7;
	background-color: var(--slot-locked);
}

/* The cooldown sweep over the icon (components/clock.rcss draws it). */
.nui-slot__cooldown
{
	left: 3dp;
	top: 3dp;
	right: auto;
	bottom: auto;
	z-index: 2;
	width: 32dp;
	height: 32dp;
	pointer-events: none;
}

/* The two effects: an active skill or item, and the end of a cooldown.
   __active and __finish keep the legacy timing (13 frames of 1/15 s looped,
   11 of 1/30 s once from the cooldown's end) and take their frames from the
   skin (--frames-pattern, P13 spec 4.6): classic gives them the legacy
   additive art (skins/classic/classic.rcss). Without art they run their
   clock and draw nothing. The modern look is code (P14 spec D3): __ring, a
   2dp accent ring inside the cell with a static glow that breathes while
   the slot is active, and __flash, a clock of its own (no art) that bursts
   at the cooldown's end (is-playing): an accent radial gradient scaling up
   by transform, hidden otherwise. Classic hides both. Under reduced motion
   the ring holds still and neither the finish effect nor the burst shows. */
.nui-slot__active, .nui-slot__finish
{
	position: absolute;
	left: 3dp;
	top: 3dp;
	pointer-events: none;
}
.nui-slot__finish
{
	z-index: 5;
}
.nui-slot__active
{
	z-index: 6;
}
@media (theme: reduced-motion)
{
	.nui-slot__finish, .nui-slot__flash
	{
		display: none;
	}
}
.nui-slot__ring
{
	display: block;
	position: absolute;
	left: 0;
	top: 0;
	right: 0;
	bottom: 0;
	z-index: 6;
	border-width: 2dp;
	border-color: var(--accent);
	border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
	pointer-events: none;
}
/* No glow on the ring: a box-shadow on the breathing ring made RmlUi compile
   its meshes again on every frame of the motion (about 4 a frame) and cost
   the idle HUD as much in classic, where the ring is hidden but its
   animation runs (P14 fix stage, NuiHudBench). The lean cell's static glow
   below stays. */
/* The ring breathes in to 0.88 of the slot and back in 0.8s, endlessly,
   only while the slot is active (is-on, bound to the same value as its
   data-if): RmlUi advances an element's animation on every update even
   while it is hidden, so an animation on every cell's ring cost the idle
   HUD each frame. By transform, not opacity: an opacity change rebuilds the
   ring's mesh on every frame of the motion, a transform nothing (an active
   auto potion pulses for as long as it is on). At rest (reduced motion) the
   ring shows whole. */
.nui-slot__ring.is-on.nui-anim
{
	animation: 0.8s sine-in-out infinite nui-slot-ring;
}
@keyframes nui-slot-ring
{
	0% { transform: scale(1); }
	50% { transform: scale(0.88); }
	100% { transform: scale(1); }
}
.nui-slot__flash
{
	display: block;
	position: absolute;
	left: 0;
	top: 0;
	right: 0;
	bottom: 0;
	z-index: 5;
	transform: scale(0);
	pointer-events: none;
}
/* The burst's 11 frames of 1/30 s: from 0.6 of the cell to 1.15, by
   transform only (an opacity change would make the gradient again on every
   frame). At rest and at is-done it has no decorator and is scaled to
   nothing, not hidden, since a hidden nui-frames runs no clock and would
   never play: RmlUi draws a decorator whatever the element's transform, so
   a gradient at rest would cost a draw every frame for as long as the slot
   keeps its cooldown's end (the quickslot feed keeps it until a rebuild).
   The gradient is made once per burst. */
.nui-slot__flash.is-playing
{
	decorator: radial-gradient(circle, var(--accent) 0%, transparent 70%);
	transform: scale(1.15);
}
.nui-slot__flash.is-playing.nui-anim
{
	animation: 0.37s cubic-out nui-slot-burst;
}
@keyframes nui-slot-burst
{
	from { transform: scale(0.6); }
	to { transform: scale(1.15); }
}

.nui-slot__count
{
	position: absolute;
	right: 1dp;
	bottom: 1dp;
	z-index: 4;
	padding: 0 3dp;
	border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
	background-color: var(--tooltip-bg);
	color: var(--text-inverse);
	font-size: var(--font-xs);
	font-weight: bold;
	line-height: 14dp;
	pointer-events: none;
}
/* The legacy digit art (components/number.rcss); classic shows it instead
   of the count. */
.nui-slot__digits
{
	display: none;
	position: absolute;
	right: 4dp;
	bottom: 3dp;
	z-index: 4;
	pointer-events: none;
}
/* The one count part of a lean grid and of a wear cell: nui-number's text
   as the count badge in the modern skins, the legacy digits in classic (its
   --number-path, skins/classic/classic.rcss). At the bottom right of the
   item, so a taller item's count sits under its lower cell. */
.nui-slot__number
{
	position: absolute;
	right: 1dp;
	bottom: 1dp;
	z-index: 4;
	pointer-events: none;
}
.nui-slot__number .nui-number__text
{
	padding: 0 3dp;
	border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
	background-color: var(--tooltip-bg);
	color: var(--text-inverse);
	font-size: var(--font-xs);
	line-height: 14dp;
	font-effect: none;
}
/* A window's key label in a cell (the taskbar's 1 to 4, F1 to F4); the
   window styles it. */
.nui-slot__key
{
	position: absolute;
	left: 3dp;
	top: 3dp;
	z-index: 4;
	pointer-events: none;
}
/* The requirement sign (CSlotWindow's sign image, at -7, +10 of the slot): a
   7dp accent triangle drawn by borders. No 3b window shows it; the gallery
   does. */
.nui-slot__sign
{
	position: absolute;
	left: -7dp;
	top: 10dp;
	z-index: 8;
	width: 0;
	height: 0;
	border-width: 4dp 0 4dp 7dp;
	border-color: transparent transparent transparent var(--accent);
	pointer-events: none;
}

/* --- The lean grid (P14 spec 4.2) --------------------------------------------- */

/* One decorator draws every resting cell base: cells of 40dp, 4dp apart, as
   a standalone .nui-slot draws its own background and border. */
.nui-slot-grid--lean
{
	position: relative;
	z-index: 0;
	decorator: nui-cells(40dp 4dp var(--radius-sm) var(--surface-sunken) var(--border) 1dp);
}
/* A lean cell draws nothing at rest (a transparent background and border
   make no geometry); it is positioned without a z-index, so the grid is its
   parts' stacking context. */
.nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot
{
	z-index: auto;
	background-color: transparent;
	border-color: transparent;
}
.nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot:hover, .nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot.is-hover
{
	background-color: var(--surface-hover);
	border-color: var(--accent);
}
.nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot.is-picked
{
	background-color: var(--slot-picked);
	border-color: var(--accent);
}
.nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot.is-target
{
	background-color: var(--slot-target);
	border-color: var(--accent);
}
.nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot.is-blocked
{
	background-color: var(--slot-blocked);
	border-color: var(--danger);
}
.nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot.is-usable
{
	background-color: var(--slot-usable);
	border-color: var(--warning);
}
.nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot.is-unusable
{
	background-color: var(--slot-unusable);
	border-color: var(--danger);
}
.nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot.is-unavailable, .nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot.is-unavailable:hover
{
	background-color: var(--slot-unavailable);
	border-color: var(--border);
}
/* An active item (an auto potion that is on): the cell itself, a 2dp
   accent border and the static glow; no motion, which would move its icon. */
.nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot.is-active
{
	border-width: 2dp;
	border-color: var(--accent);
}
/* Only lean cells carry is-active and nui-fx together; a lighter selector
   than base.rcss's no-effects rule, which takes the shadow off. */
.nui-slot.is-active.nui-fx
{
	box-shadow: 0 0 6dp var(--accent-glow);
}
/* The parts in the grid's stacking context, in the legacy order. */
.nui-slot-grid--lean .nui-slot__icon
{
	position: absolute;
	left: 3dp;
	top: 3dp;
	z-index: 1;
}
.nui-slot-grid--lean .nui-slot.is-active .nui-slot__icon
{
	left: 2dp;
	top: 2dp;
}
.nui-slot-grid--lean .nui-slot__number { z-index: 5; }
/* The bag's active part is the legacy effect's frames, which only classic
   shows (its art); the modern skins show the cell's own look above, and a
   hidden nui-frames builds no frames and runs no clock. */
.nui-slot-grid--lean .nui-slot__active
{
	display: none;
	z-index: 7;
}
.nui-slot-grid--lean .nui-slot__sign { z-index: 9; }
/* An anchor cell's item at its own size, centered in the item's area: a
   1x2 item's 64dp icon in 84dp, a 1x3 item's 96dp in 128dp; its count at
   the bottom right of that area. At rest the anchor's box is that area
   (P14b): the negative margin gives the row back its 44dp, so the box
   reaches over the cells the item covers, which take no pointer; the
   pointer anywhere over the item is over the anchor, and its hover look is
   one shape. */
.nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot--h2 { height: 84dp; margin-bottom: -44dp; }
.nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot--h3 { height: 128dp; margin-bottom: -88dp; }
.nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot.is-covered
{
	pointer-events: none;
}
.nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot--h2 > .nui-slot__icon { top: 9dp; }
.nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot--h3 > .nui-slot__icon { top: 15dp; }
/* A wider item (no legacy item is; Wave 4's grids may hold one): its icon
   at its own width, centered across its columns. */
.nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot--w2 { width: 84dp; margin-right: -44dp; }
.nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot--w3 { width: 128dp; margin-right: -88dp; }
.nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot--w2 > .nui-slot__icon, .nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot--w3 > .nui-slot__icon
{
	width: auto;
	height: auto;
}
.nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot--w2 > .nui-slot__icon { left: 9dp; }
.nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot--w3 > .nui-slot__icon { left: 15dp; }
/* While something is attached (is-attaching): every cell is one cell again
   and takes the pointer, so the footprint and the drop follow the cell
   under the pointer (P14 spec 4.4); the count keeps its place. */
.nui-slot-grid--lean.is-attaching > .nui-slot--h2, .nui-slot-grid--lean.is-attaching > .nui-slot--h3
{
	height: 40dp;
	margin-bottom: 0;
}
.nui-slot-grid--lean.is-attaching > .nui-slot--w2, .nui-slot-grid--lean.is-attaching > .nui-slot--w3
{
	width: 40dp;
	margin-right: 0;
}
.nui-slot-grid--lean.is-attaching > .nui-slot.is-covered
{
	pointer-events: auto;
}
.nui-slot-grid--lean.is-attaching > .nui-slot--w2 > .nui-slot__number { right: -43dp; }
.nui-slot-grid--lean.is-attaching > .nui-slot--w3 > .nui-slot__number { right: -87dp; }
.nui-slot-grid--lean.is-attaching > .nui-slot--h2 > .nui-slot__number { bottom: -43dp; }
.nui-slot-grid--lean.is-attaching > .nui-slot--h3 > .nui-slot__number { bottom: -87dp; }

/* --- Wave 3c (P15) ------------------------------------------------------------- */

/* A skill cell's plus button (CSlotWindow::AppendSlotButton: a CSlotButton
   at the slot's x + 1, y + 19, shown per slot; P15 spec 4.2). It is a div
   beside the cell in the cell's place, over the cell's lower left corner,
   never inside the cell: a press on it must not reach the cell, and a data
   event cannot stop its propagation. It takes the pointer, so the hit
   test's sweep counts its points as the button's (nuitool snap --sweep
   reports -3 for them), and the window binds its hover to the cell's
   tooltip, as legacy's button calls the slot window's OnOverInItem. Modern:
   a 16dp accent square with the plus glyph in the accent's text color;
   classic: legacy's btn_plus art (skins/classic/classic.rcss).

   <div class="char-skill-place" data-for="c : skills">
   	<div class="nui-slot nui-anim" ...>...</div>
   	<div class="nui-slot-button nui-anim" data-if="c.button"
   	     data-event-mousedown="skill_plus(c.slot, ev.button)"><span
   		class="nui-glyph nui-glyph--plus"><span class="nui-glyph__a"></span><span
   		class="nui-glyph__b"></span></span></div>
   </div> */
.nui-slot-button
{
	display: block;
	position: absolute;
	left: 1dp;
	bottom: 1dp;
	z-index: 10;
	box-sizing: border-box;
	width: 16dp;
	height: 16dp;
	background-color: var(--accent);
	border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
}
/* The glyph fills the button, off the text line (a 16dp inline box on a
   line of the inherited font would sit lower). */
.nui-slot-button .nui-glyph
{
	position: absolute;
	left: 0;
	top: 0;
	--glyph-ink: var(--accent-text);
}
.nui-slot-button:hover
{
	background-color: var(--accent-hover);
}
.nui-slot-button.nui-anim
{
	transition: background-color 0.1s cubic-out;
}

/* The refine window's cells (P15 spec 6.2). is-closed: a cell at or past
   the recipe's lock index (legacy shows its base image, the closed look):
   dimmed, with no hover look, a lock glyph in the middle (the window's
   markup). is-ghost: the recipe's reference icon at half its alpha
   (legacy's SetSlot with a diffuse of 0.5), no count. */
.nui-slot.is-closed, .nui-slot.is-closed:hover,
.nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot.is-closed, .nui-slot-grid--lean > .nui-slot.is-closed:hover
{
	background-color: var(--slot-unavailable);
	border-color: var(--border);
}
.nui-slot.is-closed .nui-glyph--lock
{
	position: absolute;
	left: 11dp;
	top: 11dp;
	--glyph-ink: var(--text-muted);
}
.nui-slot.is-ghost .nui-slot__icon
{
	opacity: 0.5;
}
